From 273ad7a1fab3ad325edeea734277d86200d321cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wil Taylor <ai@wiltaylor.dev>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 12:55:28 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] d3d12: Build a system-wide d3d12.dll bridge.

Turn vkd3d-proton's d3d12.dll into a replacement for the Windows system
d3d12.dll:

- Load the core only from <bridge directory>\vmlab-win3d\vkd3dcore.dll,
  never from System32\D3D12Core.dll, which is Microsoft's runtime.
- Keep the native export table. It is generated from native_exports.txt
  by gen_exports.py: vkd3d-proton implements the device and root
  signature exports; the rest are thunks that resolve, on first call,
  in the preserved native DLL vmlab-win3d\d3d12-native.dll. A missing
  native export returns a listed fallback value instead of failing the
  load, so the same bridge serves any Windows 10/11 d3d12.dll.
- Hook the native DXGI factory's CreateSwapChain* methods. Swap chains
  for vkd3d-proton queues are created by the private DXVK DXGI,
  vmlab-win3d\dxgi-vulkan.dll; other devices use native DXGI.
- If the core cannot be loaded, forward the vkd3d-proton exports to the
  native DLL, so the bridge degrades to stock behaviour.

Based on the bridge prototyped in the virtio driver-integrated-3d
experiments (libs/d3d12/main.c and native_dxgi.cpp), without its
hard-coded C:\Windows forwarder paths.
